<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch PTT says BTA, adviser did not meet.</title>
<headline>Dutch PTT says BTA, adviser did not meet.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch post and telecoms group Koninklijke PTT Nederland KV (KPN) said on Wednesday that its financial adviser Goldman Sachs had not met with Bankers Trust Australia in Australia earlier on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A spokesman for KPN retracted his earlier comment that the two parties had held a meeting.</p>
<p>&quot;There was no contact at all,&quot; he told Reuters.</p>
<p>BTA earlier said it had bought a 19.9 percent stake in TNT, the subject of a friendly A$2 billion takeover bid from KPN.</p>
<p>Fund manager BTA also said KPN's A$2.45/share cash offer was &quot;at the lower end of a range of valuations&quot; it had made.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
